{
  "_comment": [
    "The shipped identity catalog (spec §6.3). Every token here is an identifier, never prose:",
    "the locale files turn 'interest:animals' into a sentence, so a save file contains no English",
    "and a translation change cannot rewrite anybody's personality.",
    "",
    "Three different mechanisms are used deliberately and must not be confused:",
    "  ages / professions / archetypes  are GATES  - non-empty means 'only these'.",
    "  favour_archetypes / favour_personalities are WEIGHTS - a thumb on the scale, never a rail.",
    "  never_with_professions / never_with_personalities are BANS - they exist so a profile can",
    "  never infer a sensitive identity from a job or a mood. A cleric is not automatically devout",
    "  in a particular way, an outlaw is not automatically cruel, a 'sensitive' villager is not",
    "  fragile, and a nitwit is not incompetent.",
    "",
    "conflicts is symmetric: declaring one direction is enough."
  ],

